kind: baseline
question: what are 0.3.14's headline decode and prompt rates at the serving defaults on the release tarball's bloomery-serve: V4.1-Flash Q3_K_M at --place bp (RTX A6000 + RTX 3090), and K-EXAONE-2.0-750B-A37B IQ2_XXS at --place a (RTX A6000 alone)
term: decode tok/s of V4.1-Flash at D=512, the release tarball's bloomery-serve, --place bp, ctx unset
unit: tok/s
predict: 36.0..45.0
condition: one hold, tools/release/sitting.sh through just release-sitting 0.3.14 --binary portable; cells target/release-dist/cells-0.3.14.tsv; tools/ref/depth-serve.sh arms D=512 and D=4096, 2 rounds, each round a fresh server with every lever unset and ctx unset
reason: 0.3.13's sittings 6 and 7 on the same file and cards read 40.53..42.60 tok/s at D=512 (35.80..38.69 at D=4096, pp 107..126 at 512 and 338..359 at 4096) [measured]; since then the V4.1 two-card decode path with no lever set changed only by the plan's accounting (#1191 holds 53 fewer card experts on plan (a), 892 MB, under 2 % of the card set [derived: a share of the hit rate, not timed]) and the host-short context step (#1195, inert when the host is not short), so the band is 0.3.13's rows ±10 %. The EXAONE cell is read beside it with no band of its own: its only references are server timings outside a lease on a 0.3.14 pre-release tree (decode 10.4..11.0 at prompts of 24..32 ids, ctx 8192; prompt 42..48 at 64..1,077 ids, ctx 262144)
decide-in: write the rows into the release notes' tables with these conditions
decide-below: under 36.0: a lever or a plan drifted; read the plan line, the host's MemAvailable and the witness block before writing a number, compare with 0.3.13's bp rows
decide-above: beyond 45.0: read the witness block and the plan line (the room, the place) before crediting
